    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.sessions\n\n### Description\n\nI'd like to start with session by default but to have an option to skip it without loading a file. \r\nFor example\r\n`nvim \"+let g:mini_sessions_enabled = v:false\"`\r\nIt can also serve if one decides to condition session loading in init\r\nOr maybe I missed the existing option?))",
