    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This can already be done two ways (well, one and a half):\r\n- All \"runtime\" options in every 'mini.nvim' module can be [modified manually after setup to take effect](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/b0ba2b98ee63b4814fcfa7657dab9f72bc4cc7da/README.md?plain=1#L79). So in this case the most suitable way of doing this is to use `nvim -c 'lua MiniSessions.config.autoread = false'`.\r\n- Any 'mini.nvim' module have the same [disabling functionality](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/b0ba2b98ee63b4814fcfa7657dab9f72bc4cc7da/README.md?plain=1#L80). In this case you can do `nvim -c 'let b:minisessions_disable=v:true'`. That is only a half-solution because it will disable `mini.sessions` in the first loaded buffer, requiring resetting this variable or creating new buffer in order to use 'mini.sessions'.",
            "created_at": "2022-05-09T07:13:28Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/76#issuecomment-1120726815",
